's high of 42\u00b0F was the 5th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 37 since 1927, the coolest since 2023.","t_yest":"November 13: cooler than 83% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>42\u00b0F</strong> was the 5th coolest November 13 high (tied) of 37 since 1927, the coolest since 2023. The normal high for the date is 52\u00b0F, and the record is 67\u00b0F (2010). The low of <strong>29\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Westfield's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Westfield has set <strong>267 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 265 that chance alone would give, and <strong>307 record highs</strong>, close to the 266 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (122). Westfield's all-time high is 103\u00b0F, on July 6, 2010.","t_chg":"No clear change in Westfield's highs or lows","p_chg":"Across 31 complete years: Westfield's average low shows no clear change: \u22120.12\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.30 to +0.06) that includes zero. Westfield's average high shows no clear change: +0.16\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.02 to +0.34) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months; November fell. Highs rose in 5 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Westfield's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.29 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 46.2 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (70.73 in); the driest, 2016 (29.82 in). Westfield almost never sees snow (the 1991\u20132020 average is 40.7 inches a winter), so there's no snowfall chart.","show_snow":false,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 11 daily record highs, 6 daily record lows"}}